Fix Email Service & Expand Dashboard Logic
This implementation plan addresses two key requests: fixing the email/OTP service and expanding the dashboard statistics on the backend.

Proposed Changes
1. Fix Email Service & Registration Flow
Currently, the application silently returns true when the Brevo API key is not present, hiding the OTP from you during local development. Also, the OTP verification logic in the registration service was commented out, meaning anyone could register without validating their email.

server/src/config/emailconfig.js: Add a local development fallback that prints the OTP to the console so you can copy and paste it into the UI during testing.
server/src/service/users.service.js: Uncomment and restore the OTP validation in registerUser to ensure the security flow works correctly.
2. Expand Dashboard Options in the Backend
Currently, the backend dashboard stats (getDashboardStats) only counts projects and tasks where the user is explicitly the Assignee. We need to expand this to also include projects where the user is the Creator, ensuring they see all their data in the dashboard.

server/src/service/projects.service.js: Update the getDashboardStats Prisma queries to use an OR condition, fetching projects/tasks where the user is either the assignId OR the createdBy.
